# Walkthrough: SkillPilot Learning System (Phase 2)

I have successfully implemented the core Learning System for SkillPilot. This phase includes the robust modular structure for Courses, Lessons, Progress tracking, and Certificates.

## 🏗️ Core Architecture
- **Modular Design**: Using `nwidart/laravel-modules` to separate concerns.
- **Unified Auth**: Integrated Laravel Sanctum for secure API access.
- **Multi-tenancy**: Seamlessly integrated `tenant_id` filtering using global scopes and traits.

## 🚀 Key Modules & Endpoints

### 1. Courses Module
Manage course metadata, pricing, and sections.
- `GET /api/courses` - List all courses (Tenant filtered)
- `POST /api/courses` - Create new course
- `POST /api/courses/{id}/sections` - Add a curriculum section

### 2. Lessons Module
Curriculum delivery with support for multiple content types.
- `POST /api/lessons` - Add lesson to a section
- `GET /api/lessons/{id}` - Retrieve lesson content (Video/PDF/Text)

### 3. Progress Tracking
Real-time progress monitoring for students.
- `GET /api/progress/{courseId}` - Get completion percentage and lesson status
- `POST /api/progress/complete` - Mark a lesson as finished

### 4. Certificates
Automated certificate generation upon course completion.
- `POST /api/certificates/issue` - Issue a certificate (auto-generates unique serial no)
- `GET /api/certificates` - View user's earned certificates

---

